Sea and Moon by Mårten Rånge (mrange)
https://www.shadertoy.com/view/csfXzN

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper; see the note at the
top of main.metal for what was changed.

Where the licence is stated
---------------------------
This port was made from the author's own HLSL version of the shader:
https://github.com/mrange/windows-terminal-shader-gallery/blob/main/gallery/sea-and-moon/fragment-0.hlsl
(repository state 46c900b4820cadb2b46546f74f17ba20bf43b56e, checked 2026-11-11).

1. The metadata file stored beside that shader in the author's repository,
   gallery/sea-and-moon/metadata.json (lines 4 to 7), reads:

       "legal": {
         "license-expressions": ["CC0-1.0"],
         "authors": ["Mårten Rånge"]
       },

   https://github.com/mrange/windows-terminal-shader-gallery/blob/main/gallery/sea-and-moon/metadata.json

2. The header of the original Shadertoy shader (csfXzN) reads:

       // License CC0: Sea and moon
       //  Tinkering with the colors of an old shaders to make it a better fit for windows terminal

   Shadertoy does not allow automated fetching, so this header was read from
   a verbatim copy of it on https://godotshaders.com/shader/sea-and-moon/
   (a third-party Godot port, which that site labels MIT; nothing from that
   port is used here). It agrees with item 1.

The repository as a whole also carries an MIT LICENSE, "Copyright (c) 2022
Mårten Rånge". The per-shader statement in item 1 is the more specific one and
is the one used here; both come from the same author, and both allow this use.

The HLSL file itself carries no licence header. One small helper in it,
tanh_approx(), is marked "License: Unknown, author: Unknown, found: don't
remember". It is not included in this port; see the next section.

What was changed
----------------
- Removed the Windows Terminal wrapper and the blending of the terminal's text
  over the picture; the shader draws the picture only.
- Time and resolution come from iTime and iResolution; no coordinate flip is
  needed with the bottom-left origin.
- HLSL names became GLSL / Metal names; the mod() adapter and the unit2/3/4
  constants were dropped; dot(dsea, dsea) on a scalar is written dsea*dsea.
- tanh_approx() was replaced by the built-in tanh(), with its argument capped
  at 15 (Metal's tanh overflows for large inputs). Every call in this shader
  has k*h >= 25, where both give exactly 1.0; renders made with and without
  the change were identical pixel for pixel at three different times.
- The unused local d2 in sea() and the unused TAU constant were left out.
- Wave motion, colours and constants are unchanged.
- No images are shipped; the shader needs none.

